schwab-gate gate 8: reading a credential into the transcript — named credential files, and recursive searches that do not skip gitignored files [st-7lw9]

2026-08-25: `command grep -rn <desk-url> .` from the repo root printed the
untracked .env (Schwab key and secret) into an agent transcript. The Read
tool's deny list covers .env; the Bash side had nothing, and gate 4 gates
writes only. Steve chose option (a), a filename deny, on 2026-09-30.

A filename deny alone would not have caught the incident — that grep never
named the file — so gate 8 has two clauses:
  8a  a content verb (cat, head, grep, sed, jq, xxd …) in command position
      whose segment names .env, .beads-credential-key, a gate/fire key,
      tokens/, /var/lib/execd/*.json or /etc/execd/
  8b  a recursive search that does not skip gitignored files (command grep
      -r, pathed or escaped grep, egrep/fgrep, rg -u/--no-ignore) rooted at a
      tree holding a credential, with no --include
The plain grep shim skips ignored files (measured 2026-09-30: `grep -rl` does
not list .env, `command grep -rl` does), so `grep -rn x .` stays free, as do
ls, git check-ignore, .env.template and commit messages naming .env.

Measured 2026-09-30 against the live hook: all 19 new BLOCK cases ALLOW
today and BLOCK with this change; 12 new ALLOW controls pass on both; the
existing 132 cases are unchanged. Pinned in tests/test_schwab_gate_hook.py.

Known limit: a quoted '|' or ';' inside an 8a argument can split a segment;
the direction of that error is a false block, not a leak, except for
contrived quoting around the file name itself.

Prepared by Strader; landed by Steve.
